   abstract = {A two-stream approximation model of radiative transfer is used to calculate values of hemispheric canopy reflectance in the visible and near-infrared wavelength intervals. Simple leaf models of photosynthesis and stomatal resistance are integrated over leaf orientation and canopy depth to obtain estimates of canopy photosynthesis and bulk stomatal or canopy resistance. The ratio of near-infrared and visible reflectances is predicted to be a near inear indicator of minimum canopy resistance and photosynthetic capacity but a poor predictor of leaf area index or biomass. © 1985 Taylor and Francis Ltd.},
